P-S1, spec 001's shared account (spec.md Assumptions, "One account, shared with the Author's other work"; ADR 0047;
tasks.md T150 to T154). For the Author's hand only: all three files are protected (FR-012;
.claude/hooks/protected-paths.sh, infra/*budget*, infra/*iam*, and killswitch*.tf).

Built on 2026-11-12 from plain copies, never `git apply` or a write into a worktree: each of main's files by
`git show refs/heads/main:…`, edited, then `diff -u` with a/ and b/ labels. Apply it from the repository's top with
`patch -p1`, which skips this preamble.

  - infra/bootstrap/budgets.tf: h4-server-month counts every cost tagged project = h4reet-ai but Bedrock's
    services, as two `and` terms of its filter_expression (a `not` of the services, and the tag), so the Author's
    other work in the shared account never trips the server action.
  - infra/account/killswitch.tf: h4-rehearsal-server on the same filter, so tripping the rehearsal proves the real
    budget's filter reads this project's spend.
  - infra/account/iam.tf: h4-credential-audit-fn may read one parameter more, /h4reet/audit/IAM_ALLOW, the Author's
    allowlist, which stays out of the repository.

To confirm at the plan: that hashicorp/aws 6.72.0 takes `and` holding a nested `not`, and `and` holding `tags`.
After the apply, once the project tag is active: that Cost Explorer filtered on it shows the project's costs, and
that h4-server-month's actual matches; if the budget reads $0 while Cost Explorer doesn't, the key may want
`user:project`.

